{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1530647-the-black-towers-chronicle-a-draft-for-a-new-game-i-m-planing","id":1530647,"title":"The Black Towers Chronicle - A draft for a new game I'm Planing","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-12T09:18:05-08:00","id":1530647,"title":"The Black Towers Chronicle - A draft for a new game I'm Planing","content":"Hi all,<br /> <br /> I'm planning a Mage the Awakening 2nd Edition Chronicle and some feedback about this draft would be appreciated.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance.<br /> <br /> The setting is Madrid, capital city of Spain.<br /> <br /> <b>Main plot</b><br /> <br /> The players will witness during their Awakenings how a deep black &quot;something&quot; covered the watchtower, henche the name of the chronicle.<br /> <br /> My idea is that each player, each one from a different path, have a piece of something (artifact, soul stone) attached to them, most probably to their souls.<br /> <br /> What I have clear is that this was done by one of the player's mentor in secrecy, time before the player's awakening. Why? Because he distrusted other members of the Council and there was certain risk of Scelesti getting their hands on the something. By hiding pieces of it in a bunch of sleepers and by keeping them under surveillance he thought he could control of the situation.<br /> <br /> But the players awakened exactly at the same time, this weird black stuff happened and the mentor is not very talkative about it, he still things he can solve it by his own.<br /> <br /> <b>The Councilium of Madrid - Notable members</b><br /> <br /> After a crude civil war within the Pentacle a statys-quo was achieved. It was decided that members of a single Cabal will be ruling the city but in exchange, its members will resign from their ranks in their orders. They will have voice but not a vote in them.<br /> <br /> Well, meet Reina (Queen in Spanish)Hierarch, a Silver Ladder Moros and head of The Chessboard cabal. Despite her name, she is not an authoritarian figure and rules the Consilium more like an arbitrator. Magic is Mages' birthright after all and as long as status quo within the magic community is kept.<br /> <br /> Ruy is the oldest mage in Madrid, is a former Adamantine Arrow, he was the head of the Adamantine Arrow back during the civil war and after some time, he pushed vehemently for peace.<br /> Nowadays he is a Vidanti and refuses to go to Council meetings. He owns and runs a rock bar. He doesn't refuse to meet other mages in an informal way, though, young mages are welcome to ask him for some advice from time to time.<br /> <br /> <b>On the Free Council</b><br /> <br /> One of the reasons of the civil war was the restrictions of the Free council, for example, they were &quot;asked&quot; in a threatening way to surrender their artifacts and books to be kept by other Orders.<br /> After the status quo there are still some grudges but things calmed down. Most of their stuff were given back except for some items and there's still some conflict about it. They are technically separated from the Diamond but decided to form an alliance to confront external forces like the Scelesti or the Seers. <br /> <br /> Free Council members are free to join any cabal as long as they respect the Council laws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6914-javimanzano","name":"JaviManzano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6914_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T18:47:59-08:00","id":1530693,"title":"","content":"Does this have any relation to the Black Tower faction of the Adamantine Arrow ? If I remember correctly, their name came from an structure the Ungula Draconis were sworn to defend, one of the tallest towers of Atlantis, granting them a view of every harbor and thoroughfare. In a sense, it could be seen as a literal watchtower.<br /> <br /> Its one of the first things that came to mind, along with the idea of the holders of the pieces representing the black pieces in some cosmic game of chess, like in <i>No Game, No Life</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-13T01:25:19-08:00","id":1530723,"title":"","content":"There is some chess involved, indeed, but that's because the name of the ruling cabal and Reina is a member of the Awakening Gambit Legacy. She will probably have nothing to do with the player's dilemma but they might indulge in their paranoia and some political drama is always welcome.<br /> <br /> The Black Tower faction has nothing to do with this.<br /> <br /> I thought about this and I've decided that the players have some sort of soulstone attached to them and that caused these visions during their Awakenings so this might be a VERY LONG game of chess that started some millenia ago and is ending now. In fact, after some sessions when they started to get some key knowledge I plan to start the session by giving them new character sheets with different skills and in a different time (Neolitic, specifically, to use the Dark Eras) It will be a dream, or not.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6914,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6914-javimanzano","user":"JaviManzano","date":". 02-13-2024, 04:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6914-javimanzano","name":"JaviManzano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6914_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}